South American organizations are modernizing IT environments to support digital services and improve operational efficiency. Converged platforms may help enterprises simplify infrastructure management and strengthen disaster recovery. However, capital constraints, financing conditions, and uneven access to specialized technical skills can influence deployment decisions.

Middle East and Africa
Investment in digital transformation, data centers, and smart infrastructure is creating opportunities in parts of the Middle East. In Africa, businesses and public institutions may benefit from integrated platforms that reduce operational complexity and support scalable services. Infrastructure availability, financing, and technical expertise remain important factors affecting adoption.

